       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 8000 mg four times daily comes to 32,000 mg per day. That is 10 times the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen, which is 3,200 mg per day for adults in monitored settings. A dose like that could cause severe GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS toxicity.\n\nDid you mean **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day)? That is the top of the usual range. Many clinicians use 400\u2013600 mg every 6 hours (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day) for routine analgesia or anti-inflammatory use.\n\nTell me the dose you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 8000 mg, please confirm that explicitly and tell me the clinical rationale, so I can add it to the order note."
