     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 8000 mg per dose is far beyond any therapeutic use of ibuprofen. It's about 10 times the maximum daily dose, and a single 8000 mg dose is already in the range associated with serious toxicity. Four of those doses a day would very likely cause serious harm, and I don't know of any indication that would justify it.\n\nYou can still get what you need in one of these ways:\n- **A different dose:** Give me the intended dose, such as 800 mg four times daily or 600 mg every 6 hours, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **A different indication:** If you're trying to reach a particular goal, such as anti-inflammatory dosing or opioid-sparing analgesia, I can enter a standard regimen for it.\n- **Pharmacy review:** If you think there's an unusual reason for this dose, a clinical pharmacist or toxicology consult should review it before any order goes in through the normal channels."
      }
     ],
